{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And from Gudgodah, etc.</b> In Moserah you made heavy mourning over the death of Aharon, for it brought this upon you, and it seemed to you as though he died there (Talmud Yerushalmi Sotah 1; Mekhilta Exodus 15; Tanḥuma Ḥukkat); and Moses attached this reproof to the breaking of the tablets, to say that the death of the righteous is difficult before the Holy One, blessed be He, like the day the tablets were broken, and to inform you that what they said — ״נִתְּנָה רֹאשׁ״ (Numbers 14) — to separate from Him was difficult for Him, like the day they made the calf (Vayikra Rabbah 20)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:24.815962315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}